"Filter pay ways compatible with the given shipping carrier. Each carrier "
"declares which settlements it can physically perform, per kind: a BoxNow "
"locker takes a card at its terminal (PAY ON THE GO) and never courier cash, "
"while an ACS courier is the exact opposite. Has no effect without "
"``shippingKind`` — the rules are per-kind, so a carrier alone says nothing."
msgstr ""
"Filter pay ways compatible with the given shipping carrier. Each carrier "
"declares which settlements it can physically perform, per kind: a BoxNow "
"locker takes a card at its terminal (PAY ON THE GO) and never courier cash, "
"while an ACS courier is the exact opposite. Has no effect without "
"``shippingKind`` — the rules are per-kind, so a carrier alone says nothing."

#: .\pay_way\filters.py:101
msgid ""
"Filter pay ways by the shipping kind. Pair with ``shippingProviderCode`` for"
" one carrier's rules; on its own it returns only the pay ways every carrier "
"serving that kind accepts, which is what a provider-agnostic "
"``home_delivery`` checkout needs."
msgstr ""
"Filter pay ways by the shipping kind. Pair with ``shippingProviderCode`` for"
" one carrier's rules; on its own it returns only the pay ways every carrier "
"serving that kind accepts, which is what a provider-agnostic "
"``home_delivery`` checkout needs."

#: .\pay_way\filters.py:111
msgid ""
"ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 delivery country. Drops the pay ways an operator excluded"
" for that country (e.g. BoxNow PAY ON THE GO in Cyprus). Has no effect "
"without ``shippingKind``; when omitted only the every-country exclusions "
"apply."
msgstr ""
"ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 delivery country. Drops the pay ways an operator excluded"
" for that country (e.g. BoxNow PAY ON THE GO in Cyprus). Has no effect "
"without ``shippingKind``; when omitted only the every-country exclusions "
"apply."

